WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.110
Count the atoms in one
molecule of glucose:

2
00:00:03.160 --> 00:00:07.040
6 carbon, 12 hydrogen and 6 oxygen.

3
00:00:07.090 --> 00:00:08.770
Now count fructose.

4
00:00:08.820 --> 00:00:12.520
6 carbon, 12 hydrogen, 6 oxygen.

5
00:00:12.570 --> 00:00:15.730
Not one atom more, not one atom less.

6
00:00:15.780 --> 00:00:18.330
Yet they are not one
sugar under two names.

7
00:00:18.380 --> 00:00:20.380
They are two different sugars.

8
00:00:20.430 --> 00:00:23.990
So if every atom matches,
what makes them different?

9
00:00:24.040 --> 00:00:26.750
In this mission, you'll
meet the single sugars:

10
00:00:26.800 --> 00:00:29.580
the building blocks of every carbohydrate.

11
00:00:29.630 --> 00:00:32.880
Then you'll watch single sugars
join into bigger molecules,

12
00:00:32.930 --> 00:00:35.410
and see water split them apart again.

13
00:00:35.460 --> 00:00:40.750
Your mission: find out what makes two sugars
with exactly the same atoms different.
